.page sudo 1 run a command with someone else's power
.alias eiki

# SYNOPSIS
*sudo* [*-u* _USER_] [*-i* | *-s*] _COMMAND_ [_ARGUMENT_ ...]

# DESCRIPTION
`sudo` is another name for `eiki`, the judge. It runs _COMMAND_ as `root` (or as _USER_) if sudoers(5) allows the caller to; it is installed setuid root. If the rule asks for a password, the caller's own is asked for, three tries. Anyone not on the list is turned away with the traditional answer, and the refusal is written to the kernel log under the tag `Eiki`:

    reimu is not in the sudoers file.
    This incident will be reported to Eiki.

`SUDO_USER` is set to the name of the caller.

# OPTIONS
@ *-u* _USER_
    Run as _USER_ instead of root.
@ *-i*, *-s*
    Start a login shell as the target user (no command needed).

# EXAMPLES
    sudo adduser patchouli
    sudo -u marisa id

# SEE ALSO
su(1), sudoers(5), accounts(7)
